{"format":"floorplan/1","building":"DE NEVE","floor":"1","title":"De Neve Commons floor 1 (Plaza Room and Lecture Auditorium level, north part)","extent":"partial","source":{"publisher":"UCLA Conferences & Catering","what":"De Neve Plaza event-space diagram: Plaza Room salons A/B, foyer, A/V booth, Lecture Auditorium, Sycamore, Magnolia and Jacaranda rooms, Computer Labs 1 and 2 (room names, no numbers, no scale)","url":"https://conferences.ucla.edu/meeting-event-spaces/de-neve-plaza/","file":"https://conferences.ucla.edu/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/Floorplan_DeNeve.jpg","date":"2018-12 (upload date)","accessed":"2026-10-15","license":"UCLA's own page (Housing & Hospitality); no license stated"},"how":"Walls are the dark lines of the plan image; rooms are the spaces they enclose, with door gaps closed by extending each wall end up to 2 m. The plan was fitted to the ground with a similarity transform on 5 control points (west end of the Plaza Room's curved front; east end of the Plaza Room's curved front; top of the Plaza Room's curved front; NW corner of the building (west wing's north wall); NE corner of the building (east wing's north wall)).","notes":["The diagram is schematic and has no scale: it is fitted with a similarity transform on five points where its Plaza Room front and the wings' north walls meet the mapped (roof) outline; the drawn Plaza Room is narrower than the roof's curved front, so the residuals are 3 to 5 m at the curve's ends.","Floor: UCLA Space Inventory lists De Neve Commons floors 1 to 3 (P1xx, P2xx, P3xx). The Learning Center P333 is on the 3rd floor (ResLife), the four PE entrance records are on floor 2 (the plaza / front-desk level), and this level has its side wings under the plaza, so it is taken as floor 1. The plan itself gives no floor; this is an inference.","Room names come from the plan (Plaza Room Salon A/B, Lecture Auditorium, Sycamore, Magnolia, Jacaranda, Computer Lab 1/2); the plan has no room numbers, so none are recorded.","The plan is cut off at the bottom (south), so the record covers the north part of the level only; two cuts close the foyer where it opens to the outdoor stairs."],"fit":{"transform":"similarity","points":5,"max_m":4.84,"rms_m":3.31,"loo_max_m":6.78,"m_per_px":0.0888,"rot_deg":0.45,"outside_outline_max_m":2.3,"control":[{"what":"west end of the Plaza Room's curved front","px":[455.0,35.0],"ll":[34.070528,-118.450342],"res_m":4.03},{"what":"east end of the Plaza Room's curved front","px":[700.0,35.0],"ll":[34.070529,-118.450024],"res_m":4.84},{"what":"top of the Plaza Room's curved front","px":[580.0,8.0],"ll":[34.070566,-118.450193],"res_m":0.88},{"what":"NW corner of the building (west wing's north wall)","px":[320.0,150.0],"ll":[34.070479,-118.45043],"res_m":2.65},{"what":"NE corner of the building (east wing's north wall)","px":[845.0,150.0],"ll":[34.070482,-118.449937],"res_m":2.67}],"px_to_m":[[0.088845,0.000693,-529.721845],[0.000693,-0.088845,63.441509],[0.0,0.0,1.0]]},"trace":{"mode":"walls","tool":"maps/trace_plan.py","date":"2026-10-15","plan_file":"Floorplan_DeNeve_1165px.jpg","page":1,"dpi":150.0,"params":{"wall_neutral":232,"door_m":2.5,"min_room_m2":2.0,"min_wall_m":1.0,"split_on":"text","outside_m":6.0},"sealed_doors":105,"dropped":{"edge":1,"small":1307,"thin":1,"outside":0,"hand":0},"flags":[],"unplaced_labels":["Foyer"],"regularized":{"grid_deg":1.24,"rooms_snapped":31,"rooms_as_traced":6}},"checks":[],"wall_m":0.18,"rooms":[{"label":"SalonA","kind":"room","poly":[[34.070556,-118.450188],[34.070554,-118.450303],[34.070474,-118.450301],[34.070476,-118.450185]],"at":[34.070518,-118.450235]},{"label":"Salon B","kind":"room","poly":[[34.070555,-118.450187],[34.070475,-118.450185],[34.070477,-118.45007],[34.070557,-118.450072]],"at":[34.070518,-118.450138]},{"kind":"other","poly":[[34.070502,-118.450382],[34.070485,-118.450381],[34.070486,-118.450305],[34.070503,-118.450306]],"at":[34.070491,-118.450371]},{"kind":"other","poly":[[34.070504,-118.450067],